		<item>
		<title>Kalepa Raises $75M to Put AI Agents to Work Across Underwriting, Pricing, and Portfolio Management in the Insurance Industry</title>
		<link>https://www.alleywatch.com/2026/11/kalepa-raises-75m-to-put-ai-agents-to-work-across-underwriting-pricing-and-portfolio-management-in-the-insurance-industry/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[AlleyWatch]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Thu, 05 Nov 2026 15:17:30 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[#NYCTech]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AI]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[AlleyTalk]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Breaking]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Business]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Exclusive]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Finance]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Funded in New York]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Funded in the Alley]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Funding]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Funding News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Insurtech]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Interviews]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[RFC-AW]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Startups]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Venture Capital]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[IA Ventures]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Inspired Capital]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Kalepa]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Paul Monasterio]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Updata Partners]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://alleywatch.com/?p=163887</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Insurance is about to lose decades of underwriting judgment to retirement, and the industry’s answer so far has been AI that fills out forms. Kalepa wants AI to take on the work itself, and CEO Paul Monasterio says the real question is which tasks belong to people and which belong to agents. With $75M in new funding, $91M in total, he is betting insurers will want that choice across every part of the business. Find out where he draws the line.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Insurance is losing judgment faster than it can replace it; a generation of veteran underwriters is retiring, and the pricing instincts they built over decades leave with them. Rising losses and softening prices shrink the margin for error on every decision, AI-native competitors enter the market built for speed, and most insurers still apply AI to isolated administrative tasks that never touch the core calls about which risks to write and how to price them. <a href="https://funding.alleywatch.com/companies/kalepa"><strong>Kalepa</strong></a>]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
			</item>
