					<description><![CDATA[US startups raised $20.83B in October, up 71% from a year ago and down 25% from September. Four rounds of $1B or more accounted for 26% of the total, and the 43 rounds of $100M or more took 68%. We broke down who raised the money and where it went.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<div style="background: #0A1429; color: #f2f7fd; font-family: -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; padding: 28px 22px; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; border-radius: 10px;">
<p style="color: #f2f7fd; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 16px;">US startups raised $20.83B across 563 rounds in October, down 25% from September and up 71% from October 2025. Four rounds of $1B or more, from Ramp, Tenstorrent, Flapping Airplanes and Kalshi, totaled $5.35B, or 26% of the month. Series A was the surprise: its $5.11B total jumped 72% from September&#8217;s $2.97B, with three rounds of $400M or more taking $2.27B of it.</p>
<div style="background: #101F40; border: 1px solid #243C6B; border-left: 5px solid #8CCBF7; border-radius: 8px; padding: 20px 22px; margin: 24px 0;">
<div style="color: #8ccbf7; font-size: 13px; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: 1.2px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 10px;">Key Insights</div>
<ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
<li style="color: #f2f7fd; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.65; margin-bottom: 9px;"><strong>Four $1B+ rounds took 26% of capital.</strong>]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
