					<description><![CDATA[Everyone’s giving AI agents access to company data. Almost nobody is making sure they understand the business. Chord just bought Zenlytic to fix that.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Chord</strong>, the New York-based AI data platform for commerce, has acquired <strong>Zenlytic</strong>, the New York AI-powered business intelligence startup, doubling its revenue. Terms of the transaction were not disclosed. &#8220;We built Zenlytic to help enterprises get answers they can trust from their own data, with a developer-first approach to keeping business context accurate,&#8221; remarked <strong>Ryan Janssen</strong>, CEO of Zenlytic. &#8220;This transaction allows Chord to build on that work, combining our analytics engine with their data infrastructure and activation capabilities so customers can move from asking questions to acting on the answers.&#8221;</p>
<p><em>We built Zenlytic to help enterprises get answers they can trust from their own data, with a developer-first approach to keeping business context accurate. This transaction allows Chord to build on that work, combining our analytics engine with their data infrastructure and activation capabilities so customers can move from asking questions to acting on the answers. – Ryan Janssen</em></p>
<p>Founded in 2018 by <strong>Ryan Janssen</strong> and <strong>Paul Blankley</strong>]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
