					<description><![CDATA[New York startups raised $4.94B in October, the largest month for startup funding in NYC history. Ramp’s $1.85B Series G is the largest startup round in NYC history, and with Kalshi’s $1B and Modal’s $750M, three rounds took 73% of the money. Fewer deals than last October pushed the average round to $91.6M, and the 2026 total has reached $27.10B, 42% above all of 2025.]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<div style="background: #0A1630; color: #eaf2fb; font-family: -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; padding: 28px 22px; max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; border-radius: 10px;">
<p style="color: #eaf2fb; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 16px;">New York startups raised $4.94B across 54 rounds in October, the largest month for startup funding in NYC history. Capital is up 61% from September and 254% above October 2025. Ramp&#8217;s $1.85B Series G was the largest startup funding round in New York City history, and with Kalshi&#8217;s $1B and Modal&#8217;s $750M it brought the top three to $3.60B, or 73% of the month. The 2026 total now stands at $27.10B across 677 rounds, 42% above the full-year 2025 total of $19.11B with two months still to go.</p>
